    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #300\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-110-module-contract-03-12-derive-active-mo-thr_qkagi8mh47`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements module-contract issue #110: deriving the desired set of active module worker instances and reconciling them through an injected supervisor port.\n\n- Added `backend/packages/data/src/moduleWorkers.ts`:\n  - `deriveDesiredWorkerInstances(moduleRegistry, getActiveRowIds)` derives a deterministic map of desired worker instance identities from `ModuleRegistry.getWorkers()` plus a caller-injected `WorkerActiveRowIdsSource`. Each worker yields either a singleton instance (`<workerName>`) or one instance per active row (`<workerName>@<rowId>`, e.g. `semprec-mailsync@<mailboxId>`), with validation against blank or duplicate row ids.\n  - `createModuleWorkerInstanceReconciler(moduleRegistry, getActiveRowIds, supervisor)` diffs the freshly derived desired set against previously hosted instance ids and emits `start`/`stop` calls only for what changed — order-independent and idempotent.\n  - `WorkerSupervisorPort` is the only integration point for actually hosting a process; this layer stays free of systemd and queue Runner ownership, per the issue's scope.\n- Exported the new API from `backend/packages/data/src/index.ts`.\n- Added 12 unit tests in `backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/moduleWorkers.test.ts` covering singleton vs. per-row derivation, inactive-module exclusion, blank/duplicate row-id rejection, and reconciler add/remove/idempotency/deactivation behavior.\n- Rebased the branch onto `origin/develop` to include the already-merged 01/12 and 02/12 module-contract work this issue depends on.\n\nVerified this turn: full backend test suite (`pnpm test`, 30 files / 392 tests) and full backend build/typecheck (`pnpm build`, all 7 packages) both pass.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
